codec.cpp does not compile with libc++ (clang): std::malloc is used without
including <cstdlib>. GCC and Apple clang accept this through transitive
includes; libc++ does not. Found while building the C++ test suite with
clang (tests/build_and_test.sh).

--- a/src/models/chatterbox_s3g.cpp
+++ b/src/models/chatterbox_s3g.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include "chatterbox_s3g.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 #include "../ops/conv1d.h"
 #include "../ops/convtr1d.h"
